.Dd November 8, 2026
.Dt HFI 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm hfi
.Nd Intel Hardware Feedback Interface driver
.Sh SYNOPSIS
To compile this driver into the kernel,
place the following lines in your
kernel configuration file:
.Bd -ragged -offset indent
.Cd "options SCHED_MIC"
.Cd "device hfi"
.Ed
.Pp
Alternatively, to load the driver as a
module at boot time, place the following line in
.Xr loader.conf 5 :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
hfi_load="YES"
.Ed
.Pp
The module cannot be unloaded once it has attached; see below.
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver supports the Hardware Feedback Interface
.Pq HFI
found on Intel hybrid processors beginning with the 12th generation Core
.Pq Alder Lake .
The processor writes a table of per-core performance and energy-efficiency
capabilities into memory the driver provides, one table per physical
package, and raises the local APIC thermal interrupt whenever power or
thermal conditions change the table.
Each capability is a number from 0 to 255; 0 means the processor
recommends that nothing be scheduled on that core.
.Pp
The driver publishes the capabilities as dynamic scores through the
.Xr cpucap 9
layer, where the
.Xr sched_mic 4
scheduler can read them.
It therefore requires a kernel built with
.Cd "options SCHED_MIC" ,
and the module refuses to load on other kernels.
.Pp
One
.Nm
device attaches below
.Pa cpu0
and manages every package.
It reads each CPU's row index from
.Dv CPUID.06H:EDX[31:16]
on that CPU, since SMT siblings and the cores of an E-core module share a
row and the index cannot be derived from the CPU number.
Table updates are copied by the interrupt handler and published from a
taskqueue after a short delay, so a burst of updates costs one
.Xr cpucap 9
commit.
The tables are re-programmed on resume.
Intel Thread Director, the per-thread classification extension of HFI, is
not enabled.
.Pp
The driver does not attach on processors without HFI, including virtual
machines that do not expose it, or when the local APIC has no thermal
interrupt slot.
.Pp
Once a table has been handed to the processor it is kept for the rest of
the boot, because some processors keep using the pages after HFI has been
disabled.
The driver therefore cannot be detached and the module cannot be
unloaded; both fail with
.Er EBUSY .
.Sh SYSCTL VARIABLES
The following variables are available under
.Va dev.hfi.0 :
.Bl -tag -width "pkg.N.perf_changed" -offset indent
.It Va enabled
Whether the tables are programmed into the processor.
.It Va table_pages , capabilities , rows , packages
The geometry reported by CPUID: table size in 4 KB pages, capability
columns per row, rows the table can hold, and packages with a table.
.It Va commits
Score batches committed to
.Xr cpucap 9 .
.It Va delay_ms
Delay between a table update and its publication, in milliseconds
.Pq default 100 .
Also settable as a loader tunable.
.It Va summary
One line of
.Dq cpuN:row:perf/eff
for every CPU with a row.
.It Va cpu.N.edx , index , pkg , perf , eff
Per-CPU: the raw
.Dv CPUID.06H:EDX
value, the row index, the package node and the last performance and
efficiency capabilities read for that row.
An index of -1 means the CPU reported no usable row and keeps the default
score.
.It Va pkg.N.id , leader , timestamp , interrupts , updates
Per-package: the CPUID package id, the CPU that programs its MSRs, the
timestamp of the last table update, thermal interrupts seen and table
updates copied.
.It Va pkg.N.perf_changed , ee_changed
The change indications from the table header after the last update.
.El
.Pp
.Va interrupts
and
.Va updates
rising while the system is loaded show the processor really updates the
table; some processors write it only once, at boot.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr coretemp 4 ,
.Xr sched_mic 4 ,
.Xr cpucap 9
.Rs
.%A Intel Corporation
.%B Intel 64 and IA-32 Architectures Software Developer's Manual
.%V Volume 3
.%T Hardware Feedback Interface
.Re
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
driver first appeared in
.Mx 4.2 .
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Lucas Holt Aq Mt luke@foolishgames.com .
The table handling follows Intel's reference HFI driver.
.Sh BUGS
CPU hotplug is not supported.
Thread Director classes are not used.
